        "reviewed_sha": "c2cae021ba996bee9a1f30fa2011b8c47d7cf275",
        "severity": "minor",
        "evidence": "core-levi-form.lean omits three things the md asserts. (1) The (1 + O(hbar_q^2)) factors of md parts (a) and (b) are NOT encoded -- AspectSqIsEigenvalueRatio states the leading-order relation as an exact equality, so md (b) comes out as the exact identity cond = max(aperp/apar, apar/aperp)^2. (2) md (c) is encoded only as the (1)<=>(2) equivalence; clauses (3) contact non-degeneracy, (4) the observability axiom Hom_C(1, Ad(A)) = 0, and (5) clean failure of Frobenius integrability have no Lean. (3) The q > 1 restriction on md (d) is not encoded -- CoreLeviData carries no q, and QuantumPressureBound is stated without it. md (e), the q = 1 degeneration, has no encoding either.",
        "notes": "The class is re-encoded as data + named propositions and both projections are gone. CoreLeviContext previously carried lamPar, lamPerp, aPar, aPerp, cond, hbar, C0 AND md conclusions (b) and (d) as its own fields; lamPar = lamPerp = aPar = aPerp = cond = 1, hbar = C0 = 0 satisfies every field, so the binder assumed nothing, and core_levi_cond_aspect_bound / core_levi_cond_bound returned a field each. FINDING: one of the two was redundant. The old docstring said cond_aspect_bound 'carries the O(hbar_q^2) correction as an explicit bound'. It carried none -- the class already asserted cond = max lam / min lam and (aperp/apar)^2 = lampar/lamperp EXACTLY, and those two force cond = max(aspect)^2 on the nose, so the bound was 0 <= C0*hbar^2 wearing an absolute value. It is now derived. The other, md (d), is a genuine physical claim and is now an explicit hypothesis whose derived consequence (a bound on the aspect ratio) is a different statement. Bean qou-z9ws."
      }
